  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sikorsky Aircraft has $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Award activity includes 10,963 awards and an average award size of $262K. Obligations fell 40.6% year over year. Historical annual obligations show variability: FY21 was $4.9B, FY22 was $3.4B, FY23 was $5.3B, FY24 was $4.8B, FY25 was $4.8B, and FY26 is $2.9B. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $2.8B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sikorsky Aircraft with $2.5B in obligations in FY2026 to date, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $291M. Other smaller markets include Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing at $20.3M, Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $20M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $18.2M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Sikorsky Aircraft's federal business trended?",
        "body": "The company recorded $2.9B in obligations in FY26 to date. Obligations were $4.9B in FY21, $3.4B in FY22, $5.3B in FY23, $4.8B in FY24, and $4.8B in FY25. Obligations fell 40.6% year over year. Average award size in the current year is $262K across 10,963 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main government buyers for Sikorsky Aircraft?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $2.8B in FY26 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $73.7M and the Department of Justice obligated $8.2M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market with $2.5B, and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing is $291M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Sikorsky Aircraft make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Sikorsky Aircraft has $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 10,963 awards with an average award size of $262K, and obligations fell 40.6% year over year. Historical obligations were $4.9B in FY21, $3.4B in FY22, $5.3B in FY23, $4.8B in FY24, and $4.8B in FY25."
